# Installation

{{ package_name }} requires Python {{ python_versions[0] }} or newer.

{% if publish_pypi -%}
```bash
pip install {{ package_name }}
```
{%- if publish_conda %}

Or with conda:

```bash
conda install -c conda-forge {{ package_name }}
```
{%- endif %}
{%- else -%}
```bash
pip install git+https://github.com/{{ github_org }}/{{ package_name }}
```
{%- endif %}

{% if dashboard -%}
## With the dashboard

The dashboard's dependencies are optional, so that importing {{ package_name }}
in a script or notebook does not pull in a web framework:

```bash
pip install "{{ package_name }}[app]"
```

Then start it with:

```bash
{{ package_name }}-app
```

{% endif -%}
## Development versions

`main` is always the most recent release. In-progress work lives on `devel`:

```bash
pip install "git+https://github.com/{{ github_org }}/{{ package_name }}@devel"
```

Documentation for `devel` is published as the
[latest](https://{{ package_name }}.readthedocs.io/en/latest/) version;
documentation for the release is
[stable](https://{{ package_name }}.readthedocs.io/en/stable/).
